chuckcar wrote:

> I might be wrong here, but there *is* an upper limit - namely the limit
> for objects on one square. It's in the 1,000's as I recall. 

There is no upper limit on items on a square and items in a container is 
not on the square.

There are several places where an item can be:

1. Free:		Not in any list but still existing.
2. Floor:		On the dungeon floor.
3. Contained:		In some container[1].
4. Inventory:		In the hero's inventory.
5. Monster inventory:	In some monster's inventory.
6. Migrating:		Moving between levels.
7. Buried:		Underground.
8. On bill:		Unpaid items.

In all these cases except first the item is on some linked list or 
lists. These lists don't have any upper bound per se, but the amount of 
memory available to NetHack process limits how many items can be held in 
memory at any given time.

Only items on the current level either on floor or buried, in any 
container on the current level, in an inventory of the player and any 
monster on the current level, used but not paid items, migrating items, 
itrems on an inventory of migrating monsters and the items currently 
under process by the executing command are in memory, all other items in 
the dungeon complex are saved on the disk.

When the player changes a level all items on or buried on the level, in 
any container on the level and in an invetory of a monster on that level 
are saved for the exited level and loaded for the entered level. Items 
and monsters on migrating list are checked if they should be placed on 
the entered level. Items on shopping bill are removed from the bill and 
destroyed if they were used up.

